        "prompt": {
          "raw": "You are a helpful senior engineer. Answer the request directly and concretely.\n\nUser request:\nI need the full history of changes and projections off it. Key-value entity or event sourced?",
          "label": "evals/akka-sdk-key-value-entities/prompt-baseline.txt: You are a helpful senior engineer. Answer the request directly and concretely.\n\nUser request:\n{{request}}",
          "config": {}
        },
        "promptId": "3e304803a50c8734927e8af6990274b49b4247cea2e2e209cea68d65819ead49",
        "promptIdx": 0,
        "provider": {
          "id": "exec:../_provider/claude.sh",
          "label": "sonnet-baseline"
        },
        "response": {
          "output": "**Event sourced entity.** Key-value entities store only the latest state, so the history is gone. An event sourced entity persists every event, which gives you the full history. Views can consume those events to build projections.\n\n- **History:** The event journal is the source of truth, so you can replay it or add a new projection later.\n- **Projections:** A View with `@Consume.FromEventSourcedEntity` builds read models from the event stream. Consumers can also react to events.\n- **Cost:** You have to design events and a state-transition handler, and you need to plan for event schema evolution.\n\nA key-value entity can still feed a View, but only from state snapshots. You'd have to build the history yourself by writing audit rows on each update, and that's what event sourcing already does.\n\nPick key-value only if you need just the current state. If so, say so and I'll adjust."
        },
        "score": 1,
        "success": true,
